C - MEMORY
===========

Understanding how memory works.


MEMORY TYPES
------------
Stack    Local variables, fast, limited
Heap     Dynamic memory, large, manual


MALLOC - ALLOCATE MEMORY
-------------------------
int *arr = (int *)malloc(10 * sizeof(int));

Allocates 10 integers on heap.
Returns pointer to first element.


FREE - DEALLOCATE
------------------
free(arr);

Release memory back to system.
Important: Always free what you malloc.


SIZEOF OPERATOR
----------------
sizeof(int)      How many bytes
sizeof(char)     Usually 1
sizeof(double)   Usually 8


EXAMPLE
-------
int *ptr = (int *)malloc(5 * sizeof(int));
if (ptr == NULL) {
    printf("Memory allocation failed\n");
    return;
}

ptr[0] = 10;
ptr[1] = 20;

free(ptr);


COMMON ERRORS
-------------
Forgot to free → Memory leak
Free twice → Crash
Access after free → Crash
malloc failure → Crash without check


VALGRIND - CHECK LEAKS
------------------------
valgrind --leak-check=full ./program

Shows memory problems.


TIPS
----
Always check malloc returned non-NULL.
Free in reverse order of allocation.
Every malloc needs a free.
Use valgrind to find leaks.
Learn this carefully.
